cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If PyDistPilot helps your work, please cite the project repository."
title: "PyDistPilot: Python Distribution Verification CLI"
version: 0.2.0
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/muhammadsaeed-ai/pydistpilot"
abstract: >-
  A local-first Python command-line tool that builds and inspects wheel and
  source distributions, rebuilds a wheel from an sdist, smoke-tests installed
  artifacts in fresh virtual environments, exports SARIF 2.1.0, and compares
  reports against accepted baselines to detect newly introduced findings.
keywords:
  - Python packaging
  - Wheel validation
  - Source distributions
  - Release engineering
  - Continuous integration
  - Package smoke tests
